# B4b architect handoff — decision required

B4b is ready for principal architect review, but it is not eligible for unqualified approval. The two production edits share common finalization between materialized testable and supported no-testable batches, and authenticate full finalized chains by mapping typed assignments to either their rendered origin or their durable rendering rejection. Testable records retain exact accepted critic authority; rejected records retain no critic, source authority, performance candidate, or promotion path. Existing checkpoint adoption and cleanup retry required no recovery rewrite.

Independent code-quality review found no newly introduced defect. It identified C1: a reachable parent-identical exact-duplicate cannot create a canonical final record under three protected invariants. The template requires a nonempty declared changed-symbol tuple; the runtime requires the actual validation tuple to be empty when source bytes equal the parent; the record schema requires those tuples to match. B4b deliberately fails closed rather than altering a real validation stage, reclassifying the candidate as a rendering rejection, or modifying protected schemas. This means rejected-only and other canonical untestable forms are implemented, while exact-duplicate-containing batches remain unable to finish until the principal chooses an invariant correction or narrows the guarantee.

Fresh static checks passed, and read-only compatibility confirmed the actual runtime-04 19-event evaluated journal/record and actual06's unchanged five-event terminal journal. No finalized wrapper, record, checkpoint, lifecycle helper, candidate evaluation, campaign, test, model call, or external action was executed.

Review [implementation-report.md](implementation-report.md), [exact diff](implementation.diff), [verification](verification.json), [independent review](task-review.md), and [architect verification](architect-verification.json). B4c remains out of scope pending this decision.
